                <text type="synoptic_situation">A cold front will clip the far southeast on Tuesday evening, before moving out to the east overnight. A high pressure system will then move over the Bight on Wednesday, and will extend a ridge across the state as it slowly moves east into NSW by Saturday. Another cold front is then forecast to cross the state from Saturday evening into Sunday.</text>
                <text type="preamble">Wind and wave forecasts are averages. Wind gusts can be 40 per cent stronger than the forecast, and stronger still in squalls and thunderstorms. Maximum waves can be twice the forecast height.</text>
